-> Dexact and the compared prediction are both nu1(nu, gb / a0) at the SAME argument: log10(x / x) = 0 by construction, so the check cannot fail (the same construction as CFG216's C1, CFG233 section 3 / CFG217).
   Its C1 (kernel round trip through ystar) is a real check; its C3 is 'reported' with load_bearing=False and a hard-coded True; its MUTATE (every D x 1.5 raises every median by log10 1.5) is an identity of the median and cannot fail.
